necting a word, phrase, clause, or sentence with that which precedes it: a colorless particle without an exact synonym in English, but expressed approximately by ‘with, along with, together with, besides, also, moreover,’ the elements connected being grammatically coördinate.
{{smaller block|In our last conflict four of his five wits went halting off, ''and'' now is the whole man governed with one.
